// Business rules DB-01..DB-18 and version/publish invariants must be implemented in PostgreSQL/application.
// vector(768) is illustrative; confirm embedding model dimension before migration.

// IMPLEMENTATION RULES (enforce via PostgreSQL CHECK / triggers / service transactions):
// - All statuses/difficulty/skill/attempt_type/rating are closed vocabularies.
// - PUBLISHED versions are immutable (including choices, group resources, blueprint items).
// - learning_contents.current_published_version_id must point to PUBLISHED version.
// - Composite FK with nullable group_version_id only checks matching when non-null.
//   Require group_version_id for grouped questions and validate the group's identity.
// - Each test_version must pass blueprint validation BEFORE publish.
// - attempt_answers must belong to attempt's fixed question set; snapshot or test_version.
// - attempt grading is idempotent; scores are derived immutable grading snapshots.
// - Attempt expiration uses server time; media referenced by published content cannot be hard-deleted.
// - estimated TOEIC score is NOT an ETS official score.

// NOTE: Reversing < for nullable child FKs is a diagram orientation change, not a change to SQL cardinality.
// DBML Ref operators alone do not encode SQL ON DELETE, deferrability, publish guards or composite FK NULL behavior.
